# Part 2: The Good, The Bad, & The Risky  

Think about your experience with the system you chose. Answer the following prompts based on your memory (or a quick look at the app/site).  

### A. Usability "Win" (The Good)  
Describe one feature of this system that makes it easy to use.  
*(Example: "I can check out with one click without re-entering my address.")*  

### B. Security "Win" (The Good)  
Describe one feature of this system that makes it feel secure.  
*(Example: "It asks for an OTP (One-Time Password) when I log in from a new device.")*  

### C. The Friction Point (The Bad)  
Describe one security feature that you find annoying or inconvenient.  
*(Example: "The password must be super complex, and I always forget it." OR "It logs me out after 1 minute, even when I'm in the middle of reading something.")*  

### D. The Security Risk (The Risky)  
Describe one usability feature that might be a security risk.  
*(Example: "It keeps me logged in forever on a public computer." OR "It doesn't ask for a password to make small purchases.")*  

